21AUG2024 @hanoihantrakul
All Tokenizers with Suffix "unified" means I am training on all 
3 data types [vocal_music, speech, instrumental_music]

Prior to AUG2024, there were two types of tokenizers:
- Vocal Music Tokenizer trained on [vocal_music, speech]
- Instrumental Music Tokenizer trained on [instrumental_music]

The Vocal Music Tokenizers followed a naming convention of
ConformerUMM_2255_2375 to indicate dataset ID 2255 (vocal_music) 
and dataset ID 2375 (speech) were being used to train the tokenizer.

The Instrumental Music Tokenizer followed a naming convention of 
ConformerUMM_SSTK to indicate dataset ID 794 (instrumental_music) was
being used to train the tokenizer.

The suffix "unified" therefore means I am training on all 3 of these 
Data ID's [2255, 2375, 794].

See this doc https://bytedance.sg.larkoffice.com/docx/VEuadCDpzo9rFNx0DQplFSaYgAq

